cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Building an Agent Memory Layer"
message: "If you use this course or its capstone, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chaurasia
    given-names: Yash
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yash-Raw/Mem-101"
url: "https://yash-raw.github.io/Mem-101/"
abstract: >-
  A hands-on curriculum for the write path of agent memory — extraction, entity
  resolution, conflict detection, belief updating, consolidation, decay and
  governance — across 84 lessons with a runnable Python lab each and a capstone
  system, memlab, that grows across three levels. Prose is CC BY 4.0; code is MIT.
keywords:
  - agent-memory
  - long-term-memory
  - large-language-models
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - curriculum
# Both are SPDX identifiers, so the dual licence is stateable directly. Saying
# `license: MIT` with a license-url pointing at the CC BY file made the two
# fields contradict each other for anyone citing this.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
# Must equal memlab.production.release.VERSION -- validate_capstone.py checks it.
version: "0.3"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
